  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sanamala Siva Sujith Kumar vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 6 March, 2025 Aphc010109912025 In The High Court Of Andhra Pradesh At Amaravati [3457] (Special Original Jurisdiction) Thursday, The Sixth Day Of March Two Thousand And Twenty Five Present The Honourable Sri Justice Harinath.N Criminal Petition No: 2366/2025 Between: Sanamala Siva Sujith Kumar and Others ...Petitioner/Accused(S) And The State Of Andhra Pradesh ...Respondent/Complainant Counsel for the Petitioner/accused(S): 1. D Kasi Rao Counsel for the Respondent/complainant: 1. Public Prosecutor Hn,J Crl.P.No.2366 of 2025",
    "facts": "It is alleged that the accused No.1 has purchased the prohibited noxious food items from accused No.2 and that they were selling the same without license to the public. 4. It is submitted that though the petitioners are charged with the offence of purchasing noxious food items and selling them without permission, the police have registered the case and filed charge sheet in Badvel Urban Police Station in Crime No.111 of 2019 for the offences under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 and Sections 57 & 58 r/w 26, 30 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the police do not have the jurisdiction to register the case under the provisions of Penal Code and that similar matters came up for consideration before this Court in the batch of quash petitions, which were decided by this Court in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch vide order dated 27.08.2018. HN,J 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the police do not have the jurisdiction to register the case under the provisions of Penal Code and that similar matters came up for consideration before this Court in the batch of quash petitions, which were decided by this Court in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch vide order dated 27.08.2018. HN,J 6.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
